---
import { cta, site } from '../../lib/site';

// Every number on the ticket is real, hand-checkable production math:
// 200 × 6 oz = 1,200 oz = 75 lb · 200 ÷ 4 = 50 lemons · 200 × 0.25 oz = 3 lb 2 oz
// 200 × 0.5 oz = 100 oz = 6 lb 4 oz butter. Compound butter reconciles too:
// ~3.1 qt butter + ~1.5 qt capers + lemon juice ≈ 5 qt. Plate $3.41 at 31%
// food cost implies an ~$11 menu price — a healthy caterer's number.
const ticket = {
	shop: [
		{ item: 'Chicken breast', qty: '75 lb' },
		{ item: 'Lemons', qty: '50 ea' },
		{ item: 'Capers', qty: '3 lb 2 oz' },
		{ item: 'Butter, unsalted', qty: '6 lb 4 oz' }
	],
	prep: [
		{ item: 'Pound + portion 6 oz', qty: '200 ct' },
		{ item: 'Caper-lemon butter', qty: '5 qt' }
	]
};
---

<section class="container-page pt-14 pb-section lg:pt-24">
	<!-- The largest type on the page states a bad moment, not a category and not a
	     credential. Three things moved here, all measured rather than guessed:

	     1. The old h1 ("The kitchen brain for caterers. Built by a chef, not a
	        software company.") spent half the page's biggest type on who built it.
	        The CTA arrived at 539px; the page did not name a problem until 1319px.
	        A reader was asked to book 780px before anything was shown to be wrong.
	     2. "Kitchen brain" is the repo's own name for the project — it is in
	        CLAUDE.md and in the booking URL — and no working caterer says it. Prep
	        sheet, shopping list, plate cost name things they hold; a kitchen brain
	        names nothing. It stays the product's internal identity, out of the h1.
	     3. The bad moment is the quote call, not the Thursday recount. Both are
	        real, but the recount is the TIME cost and the quote is the MONEY, and
	        the page already spends its problem section on arithmetic. This claim
	        also has the property a headline needs: a caterer either recognises the
	        season that stayed busy and made nothing, or he does not and leaves.
	        It is on the page today as the third of five features, at 2,950px.

	     The provenance claim is demoted, not lost: it rides in the eyebrow, and
	     FROM THE CHEF earns it properly further down instead of asserting it here. -->
	<p class="anim-enter eyebrow">
		Back-of-house software for small caterers &amp; meal-prep kitchens · built by a chef
	</p>
	<h1 class="anim-enter mt-5 max-w-[21ch] text-display font-semibold" style="--enter-delay: 80ms">
		The money is decided on the phone, months before anybody cooks.
	</h1>

	<div class="mt-10 grid items-start gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[7fr_5fr] lg:gap-10">
		<div>
			<p class="anim-enter max-w-xl text-lede text-ink-soft" style="--enter-delay: 180ms">
				Somebody asks what you would do 180 head for, and you say a number that sounds
				about right. Type in the menu and the guest count instead: it hands you the plate
				cost, the shopping list and the prep sheet, so you know the food cost before you
				say the number. Keep everything else you already use.
			</p>
			<a href={cta.href} class="anim-enter btn-primary mt-9" style="--enter-delay: 260ms">{cta.label}</a>
			<!-- "Free while I build it out" is the strongest risk-reducer on the page
			     and it used to live in BOOK A DEMO at 91% scroll depth, where almost
			     nobody reached it. It belongs beside the button being asked for. -->
			<p class="anim-enter mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft" style="--enter-delay: 300ms">
				15 minutes · bring one real order · nothing to install · free while I build it out
			</p>
			<!-- One of exactly two things here that a funded competitor cannot copy,
			     and it was buried in WHY US at two-thirds scroll depth. It costs a
			     line to say and it is checkable on the spot, which is the point. -->
			<p class="anim-enter mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft" style="--enter-delay: 320ms">
				Rather talk? Call <a
					href={site.phoneHref}
					class="font-medium text-green-deep underline decoration-current underline-offset-4"
					>{site.phone}</a
				>. I pick up.
			</p>
		</div>

		<!-- The signature element: one order becoming production lists, set as the
		     kitchen ticket it would print on. Mono is the ticket's native voice. -->
		<figure
			aria-label="Sample: one order turned into a shopping list, prep sheet, and plate cost"
			class="anim-enter-settle justify-self-center lg:-mt-6 lg:justify-self-end"
			style="--enter-delay: 360ms"
		>
			<div
				class="w-full max-w-[19.5rem] rotate-[1.5deg] bg-cream px-5 py-5 font-mono text-[0.8125rem] leading-normal text-ink shadow-ticket sm:max-w-[21rem]"
			>
				<!-- Punched hole — the wordmark's diamond, cut out of the ticket. -->
				<div
					class="mx-auto mb-4 size-3.5 rotate-45 bg-offwhite shadow-[inset_0_1px_2px_rgb(31_36_33/0.18)]"
				>
				</div>

				<div class="flex justify-between gap-4 font-semibold">
					<span>ORDER #117</span>
					<span>SAT · 6 PM</span>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-1">Chicken piccata · 200 guests</p>

				<hr class="my-4 border-t border-dashed border-ticket-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

				<p class="font-semibold text-amber-deep">SHOP</p>
				<ul role="list" class="mt-1.5">
					{
						ticket.shop.map((row) => (
							<li class="flex justify-between gap-4">
								<span>{row.item}</span>
								<span class="sr-only">: </span>
								<span class="whitespace-nowrap">{row.qty}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>

				<hr class="my-4 border-t border-dashed border-ticket-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

				<p class="font-semibold text-amber-deep">PREP</p>
				<ul role="list" class="mt-1.5">
					{
						ticket.prep.map((row) => (
							<li class="flex justify-between gap-4">
								<span>{row.item}</span>
								<span class="sr-only">: </span>
								<span class="whitespace-nowrap">{row.qty}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>

				<hr class="my-4 border-t border-dashed border-ticket-rule" aria-hidden="true" />

				<div class="flex justify-between gap-4 font-semibold">
					<span>PLATE $3.41</span>
					<span class="sr-only">· </span>
					<span>FOOD COST 31%</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figcaption class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-ink-soft lg:text-right">
				A sample order. One in, every list out.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>
